# CODEOWNERS — required review ownership for security-sensitive surfaces.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES: it requires the listed owner's review before a pull
# request that touches a matching path can merge (when "Require review from Code
# Owners" is enabled as a branch-protection rule on the protected branch). It is
# a review gate on changes to these files.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DO: it does NOT restrict which git ref a
# `workflow_dispatch` run may execute from. `workflow_dispatch` resolves the
# workflow definition from the dispatched ref, so anyone with write access can
# still push a branch with the egress-probe steps deleted and run the signing
# workflow from it, minting a receipt, without any CODEOWNERS review of that
# branch. Closing that hole requires a deployment-branch restriction on the
# `sandbox-production` environment (GitHub environment settings, outside this
# repository) — the owner's action, not this file's.
#
# Owner handle is the repository owner; replace with a team (@org/team) if one
# is created.

